                <pb facs="0895" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/3–2147: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-21">March 21, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> A–458. Reference Embassy’s secret A–404, March 7, 1947.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d572-f1"/> Effective 2359 hours, March 15, 1947, Italian Military
                    Affairs Section, AFHQ, was abolished. The Land, Naval and Air Forces Sub
                    Sections have now become Italian Land Forces, Italian Naval and Italian Air
                    Forces Branches of AFHQ, respectively.</p>
                <p>Admiral Stone terminated his official connection with AFHQ as Chief of the
                    Italian Military Affairs Section on March 15, 1947.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dunn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
